ve been coming forward  since the beginning of the conflict uh  according to the u.n uh  more than a hundred more than one  million people are facing famine and  tigra alone the conflicts i'm in amhara  region and desi the conflicts where  we're seeing is overwhelming the need is  uh huge and it's also in afari region  the government will be in a very  challenged position to address some of  the challenges the country is facing and  this conflict is also pushing away uh  some of the foreign investment that have  been important to ethiopia's building a  new image uh moving from an independent  nation to an economy that's respected so  the prime minister will be busy from day  one i would suspect i bet samuel gatatu  then ethiopia based journalist speaking  to us from desi thanks so much samuel
 

